    {
      "id": "a1-u01-d02-t01",
      "before": "a1-u01-d02-e01",
      "title": { "en": "sz and cz" },
      "body": { "en": "*Sz* sounds like the sh in \"shop\" and *cz* like the ch in \"chalk\". Both are a little harder than in English, said with the tip of the tongue further back. Each pair of letters is one sound: *proszę*, *smacznego*." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u01-d02-t02",
      "before": "a1-u01-d02-e09",
      "title": { "en": "ż and rz" },
      "body": { "en": "*Ż* and *rz* spell the same sound, like the s in \"measure\": *może*, *dobrze*. After *p*, *t*, *k* and *ch*, *rz* is said like *sz*, so *przepraszam* starts \"pshe\". When you type, the letters with marks are on the row just above your keyboard." }
    }
  ],
